1
00:00:00,840 --> 00:00:02,090
♪

2
00:00:02,590 --> 00:00:04,510
[ÖGEDEI]
Thanks to your lovely earrings,

3
00:00:04,590 --> 00:00:07,680
I have learned that all
is functioning as it should.

4
00:00:12,940 --> 00:00:14,310
[Möge breathes softly]

5
00:00:14,390 --> 00:00:16,150
[ÖGEDEI]
I have to wonder, though...

6
00:00:16,770 --> 00:00:18,730
Will people come
to see it my way

7
00:00:18,860 --> 00:00:20,980
after we have defeated
all the Jin?

8
00:00:27,580 --> 00:00:31,490
[MÖGE] Honestly, I don't have
any idea what he's thinking.

9
00:00:32,290 --> 00:00:33,250
Hm?

10
00:00:33,330 --> 00:00:36,000
[gasps] The slave girl's gone?

11
00:00:36,080 --> 00:00:37,000
Ah!

12
00:00:37,710 --> 00:00:38,750
[exclaims]

13
00:00:39,130 --> 00:00:41,840
Ugh, did she get lost again?

14
00:00:42,010 --> 00:00:43,760
Lady Möge!

15
00:00:45,050 --> 00:00:47,720
[♪ opening theme song playing]

16
00:00:55,390 --> 00:00:57,560
JAADUGAR

17
00:02:20,100 --> 00:02:21,940
[Qadaq grunts]

18
00:02:22,650 --> 00:02:25,150
-Hey, Fatima.
-[Sitara gasps, sighs]

19
00:02:25,230 --> 00:02:27,280
-So this is where you were.
-[gasps softly]

20
00:02:28,070 --> 00:02:30,360
-How dare you run away!
-[Sitara squeals]

21
00:02:30,450 --> 00:02:33,370
Qadaq! You have to help me.

22
00:02:33,450 --> 00:02:34,830
[BOTH] Lord Chinqai?

23
00:02:34,910 --> 00:02:37,370
You can write in Uyghur, right?

24
00:02:37,500 --> 00:02:38,790
[both gasp]

25
00:02:38,870 --> 00:02:40,460
♪

26
00:02:43,500 --> 00:02:44,750
[MAN]
Take care of these as well.

27
00:02:44,840 --> 00:02:47,050
Uh... there's no end in sight.

28
00:02:47,670 --> 00:02:48,970
I'm sorry about this.

29
00:02:49,470 --> 00:02:51,930
Every item
the Great Kha'an purchased

30
00:02:52,010 --> 00:02:54,220
has to be recorded
in our registers.

31
00:02:55,350 --> 00:02:56,890
So why am I here?

32
00:02:57,020 --> 00:02:59,230
Isn't this considered
a man's job?

33
00:02:59,310 --> 00:03:01,100
Just be quiet and get to work.

34
00:03:01,190 --> 00:03:04,060
Many Mongols have never
really had a strong affinity

35
00:03:04,150 --> 00:03:05,570
for reading and writing.

36
00:03:05,650 --> 00:03:07,990
Thus we're short on scribes.

37
00:03:08,070 --> 00:03:09,280
[Sitara gasps] Books!

38
00:03:09,360 --> 00:03:10,570
[both laugh]

39
00:03:10,700 --> 00:03:12,240
Who'll even read these?

40
00:03:13,030 --> 00:03:15,280
This one is by Jabir ibn Hayyan.

41
00:03:15,370 --> 00:03:18,250
-Huh?
-Uh... Oh, nothing.

42
00:03:18,410 --> 00:03:20,330
♪

43
00:03:23,920 --> 00:03:24,840
[Sitara gasps]

44
00:03:24,920 --> 00:03:28,590
Mistress, why is this book
hidden away among the others?

45
00:03:29,380 --> 00:03:33,890
Oh, you have quite a keen eye.
This one's by Jabir.

46
00:03:33,970 --> 00:03:35,850
He lived in Tus long ago.

47
00:03:36,890 --> 00:03:39,890
But I'm afraid it's not
the most reputable of tomes.

48
00:03:40,940 --> 00:03:42,400
What's the subject of his book?

49
00:03:44,850 --> 00:03:47,320
[chuckles] It's alchemy.

50
00:03:48,360 --> 00:03:49,940
[Sitara gasps]

51
00:03:51,190 --> 00:03:52,400
What's that about?

52
00:03:52,990 --> 00:03:54,530
[SITARA]
It details how one can heat

53
00:03:54,620 --> 00:03:56,240
and mix various substances,

54
00:03:56,320 --> 00:03:58,240
such as minerals,
to prepare...

55
00:03:59,040 --> 00:04:00,200
an al-iksir.

56
00:04:00,960 --> 00:04:02,540
An "al-iksir"?

57
00:04:02,620 --> 00:04:03,790
And what is that?

58
00:04:03,870 --> 00:04:05,290
It's a kind of cure-all,

59
00:04:05,380 --> 00:04:07,090
at least I think
that's what it is.

60
00:04:07,500 --> 00:04:08,840
I'm not quite sure.

61
00:04:09,300 --> 00:04:10,880
-[MÖGE] A cure-all?
-[ALL] Huh?

62
00:04:11,670 --> 00:04:12,800
[SITARA] Lady Möge!

63
00:04:12,930 --> 00:04:15,720
Do you mean a medicine
that can cure any ailment?

64
00:04:15,800 --> 00:04:16,970
[Sitara whimpers]

65
00:04:17,100 --> 00:04:18,010
Huh?

66
00:04:20,890 --> 00:04:22,230
[TÖREGENE] This is Fatima.

67
00:04:22,310 --> 00:04:24,770
She is one
of my most faithful attendants,

68
00:04:24,850 --> 00:04:26,610
Boraqchin Khatun.

69
00:04:28,230 --> 00:04:29,980
[SITARA]
So this is the chief empress

70
00:04:30,070 --> 00:04:31,190
of the Mongol Empire...

71
00:04:32,610 --> 00:04:34,030
The Great Khatun.

72
00:04:34,900 --> 00:04:37,660
Why have I been brought out here
to meet her like this?

73
00:04:37,990 --> 00:04:40,580
Listen, Boraqchin,
this girl here says

74
00:04:40,660 --> 00:04:42,120
that she is able
to concoct a cure-all.

75
00:04:42,910 --> 00:04:44,040
A danyao?

76
00:04:44,120 --> 00:04:45,210
Huh?

77
00:04:45,420 --> 00:04:49,920
I, uh... I'm sorry, but I'm
not sure what this is about,

78
00:04:50,460 --> 00:04:51,760
because all I said

79
00:04:51,840 --> 00:04:54,510
is that I'm able to read books
written in Arabic.

80
00:04:55,130 --> 00:04:57,050
-[MÖGE] You what?
-Möge.

81
00:04:57,140 --> 00:04:58,510
[MÖGE] Uh, but...

82
00:04:58,680 --> 00:05:01,010
-That is all. Take your leave.
-[Möge groans]

83
00:05:01,600 --> 00:05:03,890
[BORAQCHIN]
Sorry for making you come here.

84
00:05:04,480 --> 00:05:05,850
[sheep bleating]

85
00:05:07,190 --> 00:05:09,230
So what was all of that about?

86
00:05:09,310 --> 00:05:10,520
Who knows?

87
00:05:11,400 --> 00:05:12,860
-[MÖGE] Hold on!
-[BOTH] Uh?

88
00:05:12,940 --> 00:05:14,070
[SITARA] Lady Möge?

89
00:05:14,150 --> 00:05:17,030
[MÖGE] Say, there's something
I wanted to discuss with you.

90
00:05:17,530 --> 00:05:20,620
The whole reason I asked you
to come out here. [sighs]

91
00:05:21,740 --> 00:05:23,160
Please leave us.

92
00:05:23,250 --> 00:05:25,250
[birds chirping]

93
00:05:26,750 --> 00:05:28,540
[MÖGE] Someone's been
administering poison

94
00:05:28,630 --> 00:05:30,340
-to Boraqchin.
-[Sitara gasps]

95
00:05:30,420 --> 00:05:32,050
[MÖGE] You could see
how emaciated she was,

96
00:05:32,130 --> 00:05:34,010
and all the sores
all over her skin.

97
00:05:34,090 --> 00:05:37,220
Who did this?
Why would they do such a thing?

98
00:05:37,800 --> 00:05:40,430
[MÖGE] I'm not certain,
and I can't prove it.

99
00:05:41,010 --> 00:05:43,640
But I think the culprit
is Boraqchin's physician.

100
00:05:44,230 --> 00:05:46,940
Some time ago,
the Daoists engaged

101
00:05:47,020 --> 00:05:49,150
in a sacred tradition
known as waidan.

102
00:05:49,690 --> 00:05:50,860
What's waidan?

103
00:05:50,940 --> 00:05:53,190
[PHYSICIAN] By combining
the likes of sulfur,

104
00:05:53,320 --> 00:05:55,240
quicksilver, and sandarac,

105
00:05:55,320 --> 00:05:58,070
an elixir called
"danyao" can be created.

106
00:05:58,150 --> 00:06:00,950
It was believed
that after ingesting danyao,

107
00:06:01,030 --> 00:06:04,830
one's body would transform
and become immortal like gold.

108
00:06:04,910 --> 00:06:06,120
Was it really true?

109
00:06:06,250 --> 00:06:07,330
Sadly, no.

110
00:06:07,870 --> 00:06:10,170
Many of the ingredients
were highly poisonous,

111
00:06:10,250 --> 00:06:12,090
shortening the lives
of all who used it.

112
00:06:12,630 --> 00:06:13,880
For that reason,

113
00:06:13,960 --> 00:06:16,840
this archaic practice
was abandoned centuries ago.

114
00:06:17,340 --> 00:06:18,590
He said poison.

115
00:06:18,680 --> 00:06:20,470
I'm sure that's the word
I heard him utter.

116
00:06:20,550 --> 00:06:23,060
Unfortunately,
it isn't much to go on.

117
00:06:23,140 --> 00:06:26,180
If it worries you so,
simply keep the physician away.

118
00:06:26,270 --> 00:06:27,600
As Great Khatun,

119
00:06:27,690 --> 00:06:30,100
surely it would be simple
to replace him.

120
00:06:30,480 --> 00:06:31,480
Töregene.

121
00:06:31,560 --> 00:06:33,360
[TÖREGENE]
Let us return, Fatima.

122
00:06:33,440 --> 00:06:34,570
[SITARA] Um, right.

123
00:06:35,740 --> 00:06:36,990
[exhales softly]

124
00:06:38,740 --> 00:06:40,320
[insects trilling]

125
00:06:41,200 --> 00:06:43,030
[TÖREGENE] Neither one of us
should get involved

126
00:06:43,120 --> 00:06:44,580
with such an eerie woman.

127
00:06:44,660 --> 00:06:47,040
[sighs deeply] How harrowing.

128
00:06:47,950 --> 00:06:50,210
This was the first time
I'd seen the Great Khatun,

129
00:06:50,290 --> 00:06:51,500
and I couldn't help noticing

130
00:06:51,580 --> 00:06:54,380
she's considerably older
than Emperor Ögedei.

131
00:06:54,500 --> 00:06:56,840
You're right. She used
to be his stepmother.

132
00:06:56,920 --> 00:06:57,880
Huh?

133
00:06:57,960 --> 00:06:59,180
[TÖREGENE] Years ago,

134
00:06:59,260 --> 00:07:02,140
Boraqchin and Möge
were married to Genghis Khan,

135
00:07:02,260 --> 00:07:04,810
then Ögedei inherited them
as wives.

136
00:07:04,890 --> 00:07:05,810
[Sitara gasps]

137
00:07:06,430 --> 00:07:08,020
So the two of them
have known each other

138
00:07:08,100 --> 00:07:09,600
for quite a long time then.

139
00:07:09,890 --> 00:07:11,270
When the father dies,

140
00:07:11,350 --> 00:07:14,650
all his wives go to his son,
except for the birth mother.

141
00:07:15,110 --> 00:07:17,320
It's a common arrangement here.

142
00:07:18,110 --> 00:07:19,190
[Töregene sighs]

143
00:07:20,610 --> 00:07:22,110
Boraqchin...

144
00:07:22,490 --> 00:07:24,320
[coughing]

145
00:07:24,820 --> 00:07:26,240
[TÖREGENE] She has no sons,

146
00:07:26,330 --> 00:07:28,870
and she doesn't come
from a large family.

147
00:07:29,290 --> 00:07:30,790
Truth be told,

148
00:07:30,920 --> 00:07:34,210
I don't have any idea
how she became Great Khatun.

149
00:07:37,210 --> 00:07:40,010
[PHYSICIAN] It was believed
that after ingesting danyao,

150
00:07:40,130 --> 00:07:44,220
one's body would transform
and become immortal like gold.

151
00:07:44,300 --> 00:07:46,390
That sounds
exactly like alchemy.

152
00:07:46,470 --> 00:07:47,560
Who knew they had

153
00:07:47,640 --> 00:07:49,230
something so similar
in the east?

154
00:07:50,480 --> 00:07:52,190
An immortal body.

155
00:07:53,060 --> 00:07:54,150
A danyao?

156
00:07:55,270 --> 00:07:56,360
[Sitara gasps]

157
00:07:58,150 --> 00:08:01,570
I wonder if it's... an al-iksir.

158
00:08:02,650 --> 00:08:06,620
The ingredients
are quicksilver, sulfur...

159
00:08:07,240 --> 00:08:09,910
And what were
the other substances again?

160
00:08:11,790 --> 00:08:12,710
[rustling]

161
00:08:12,790 --> 00:08:14,210
-[SITARA] Lady Töregene.
-Huh?

162
00:08:14,830 --> 00:08:17,630
Once more, let's go meet
with the Great Khatun.

163
00:08:17,710 --> 00:08:20,340
Huh? Why is that?

164
00:08:20,920 --> 00:08:22,010
[Sitara chuckles softly]

165
00:08:22,630 --> 00:08:23,760
[Töregene grunts]

166
00:08:24,680 --> 00:08:26,470
You have something
in mind, don't you?

167
00:08:27,100 --> 00:08:28,180
Mm-hmm.

168
00:08:29,060 --> 00:08:30,890
I'd like you
to lend me your power.

169
00:08:30,980 --> 00:08:32,430
Please, Lady Töregene.

170
00:08:34,480 --> 00:08:35,650
[birds chirping]

171
00:08:36,690 --> 00:08:37,940
[SITARA] Al-iksir.

172
00:08:38,570 --> 00:08:41,070
It's a remedy
that renders one immortal.

173
00:08:41,610 --> 00:08:42,820
For generations now,

174
00:08:42,900 --> 00:08:45,490
it's lain at the very heart
of Persian alchemy.

175
00:08:45,570 --> 00:08:46,990
-[Möge gasps]
-[SITARA] Of course,

176
00:08:47,120 --> 00:08:49,700
I cannot prepare
such a thing by myself.

177
00:08:50,330 --> 00:08:53,410
That said, if you were to
assist me, Great Khatun,

178
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:55,250
I could.

179
00:08:55,880 --> 00:08:57,590
Why is there talk of this again?

180
00:08:57,670 --> 00:09:01,050
Because I believe
it's you who's been seeking it.

181
00:09:02,050 --> 00:09:03,130
Am I wrong?

182
00:09:03,590 --> 00:09:04,510
[Boraqchin grunts]

183
00:09:04,590 --> 00:09:06,220
Wait. Is that really true?

184
00:09:07,140 --> 00:09:08,930
From the moment I laid eyes
on you,

185
00:09:09,010 --> 00:09:10,180
there was something
that struck me.

186
00:09:10,260 --> 00:09:13,560
If I may surmise,
based on your appearance...

187
00:09:14,560 --> 00:09:17,770
Have you been ingesting
rahj al-gar by any chance?

188
00:09:17,860 --> 00:09:20,230
[MÖGE] What's rahj al-gar?

189
00:09:21,230 --> 00:09:22,570
[SITARA] It's a red stone

190
00:09:22,650 --> 00:09:24,450
that can be found
in volcanoes.

191
00:09:24,530 --> 00:09:25,570
And in the east,

192
00:09:25,650 --> 00:09:27,870
I've been told they refer to it
as "sandarac."

193
00:09:27,950 --> 00:09:28,910
[Boraqchin gasps]

194
00:09:28,990 --> 00:09:30,530
So I was right.

195
00:09:30,990 --> 00:09:33,040
In al-iksir and danyao,

196
00:09:33,120 --> 00:09:34,410
rahj al-gar is regarded

197
00:09:34,500 --> 00:09:36,790
as an essential ingredient,
after all.

198
00:09:37,630 --> 00:09:39,130
According
to the ancient physician

199
00:09:39,210 --> 00:09:40,710
named Hippocrates,

200
00:09:40,790 --> 00:09:43,090
rahj al-gar does have
medicinal effects

201
00:09:43,170 --> 00:09:44,800
in small doses.

202
00:09:44,920 --> 00:09:48,430
Although, it's poisonous
with continued use,

203
00:09:48,510 --> 00:09:50,390
causing loss of appetite,

204
00:09:50,470 --> 00:09:53,310
lesions on the skin,
and the growth of tumors,

205
00:09:53,930 --> 00:09:56,770
which is what you
seem to be suffering from.

206
00:09:56,850 --> 00:09:59,310
So my fear that you were
slowly being poisoned

207
00:09:59,400 --> 00:10:00,690
is completely unfounded,

208
00:10:00,820 --> 00:10:02,650
and you chose
to ingest it yourself?

209
00:10:02,730 --> 00:10:04,490
Goodness, Möge.

210
00:10:04,610 --> 00:10:06,860
Is that honestly
what you were thinking?

211
00:10:07,360 --> 00:10:08,820
Fatima, right?

212
00:10:08,910 --> 00:10:11,910
You should take a look inside
the drawers on that shelf.

213
00:10:15,160 --> 00:10:16,750
There's the rahj al-gar.

214
00:10:16,830 --> 00:10:19,210
Why were you taking
such a harmful thing?

215
00:10:19,830 --> 00:10:20,960
[Boraqchin sighs]

216
00:10:23,590 --> 00:10:26,170
To become immortal. Was that it?

217
00:10:27,220 --> 00:10:28,170
[Boraqchin grunts]

218
00:10:29,340 --> 00:10:30,300
[MÖGE] Huh?

219
00:10:30,390 --> 00:10:33,810
Yes, that's right.
I'm not a young woman anymore.

220
00:10:34,390 --> 00:10:36,140
I'd like to live a long life.

221
00:10:36,230 --> 00:10:37,520
Mistress Boraqchin.

222
00:10:38,100 --> 00:10:40,980
[SITARA] If you wouldn't mind,
please ingest this.

223
00:10:41,650 --> 00:10:43,650
Its medicine will cure you.

224
00:10:44,320 --> 00:10:45,360
[ALL] Huh?

225
00:10:47,280 --> 00:10:48,320
[breathes softly]

226
00:10:55,580 --> 00:10:57,710
Tell me, what is this?

227
00:10:57,790 --> 00:11:00,250
-A Jada stone.
-Jada stone?

228
00:11:00,330 --> 00:11:02,920
I thought you were not supposed
to ingest Jada stones.

229
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:06,550
You're wrong. It's called
a bezoar stone in Persia,

230
00:11:06,670 --> 00:11:08,630
where it has been recognized
as an antidote.

231
00:11:09,170 --> 00:11:11,590
I assume you haven't put a curse
on this, right?

232
00:11:11,680 --> 00:11:14,140
Is this the face of someone
who wishes you ill?

233
00:11:14,260 --> 00:11:15,180
[Töregene groans]

234
00:11:15,260 --> 00:11:16,260
[BORAQCHIN] Hm.

235
00:11:24,360 --> 00:11:25,820
[Boraqchin coughs]

236
00:11:26,650 --> 00:11:29,030
After you've recovered
and are feeling better,

237
00:11:29,110 --> 00:11:30,490
please summon us here again.

238
00:11:31,530 --> 00:11:34,990
We'll talk more
of the al-iksir, if you wish.

239
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:39,830
[SITARA]
Thank you very much.

240
00:11:39,910 --> 00:11:41,830
[TÖREGENE]
But I haven't done anything.

241
00:11:41,920 --> 00:11:42,830
[SITARA] Of course you have.

242
00:11:43,580 --> 00:11:45,090
If you hadn't been able to find

243
00:11:45,170 --> 00:11:47,420
those Persian physicians
who spoke with us,

244
00:11:47,550 --> 00:11:50,340
I never would have learned
about the rahj al-gar.

245
00:11:51,630 --> 00:11:53,640
[TÖREGENE]
What'll you do about Chagatai?

246
00:11:53,720 --> 00:11:55,390
[SITARA] I think we may
have been rushing things

247
00:11:55,470 --> 00:11:57,640
by assuming we should
approach him right away.

248
00:11:58,470 --> 00:11:59,890
At this point,

249
00:11:59,980 --> 00:12:02,850
by just focusing on earning
the Great Khatun's trust,

250
00:12:03,350 --> 00:12:05,440
a path will reveal itself.

251
00:12:05,820 --> 00:12:08,230
One for us both, I hope.

252
00:12:09,110 --> 00:12:10,280
Yes.

253
00:12:11,150 --> 00:12:12,530
Absolutely.

254
00:12:14,280 --> 00:12:16,830
SUMMER, A.D. 1230

255
00:12:21,870 --> 00:12:23,250
[SITARA (ADULT)]
Shortly thereafter,

256
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:26,790
the Mongol Emperor
embarked on an expedition

257
00:12:26,880 --> 00:12:28,750
against the Jin dynasty.

258
00:12:34,510 --> 00:12:37,600
SHANXI REGION - HOUSE OF ÖGEDEI
FRONT-LINE CAMP

259
00:12:40,220 --> 00:12:43,140
You can put those
right over there for now.

260
00:12:43,270 --> 00:12:45,400
-[BORAQCHIN] Möge.
-[both gasp]

261
00:12:45,480 --> 00:12:46,810
[MÖGE] Boraqchin!

262
00:12:46,900 --> 00:12:48,190
-[Kirgistani exclaims]
-You're well enough

263
00:12:48,270 --> 00:12:50,360
to be walking outside?
[chuckles]

264
00:12:50,480 --> 00:12:52,570
-Yes, so it seems.
-[Kirgistani exclaims]

265
00:12:52,650 --> 00:12:54,900
-It's all thanks to Fatima.
-Yeah!

266
00:12:56,070 --> 00:12:57,450
[BORAQCHIN] Indeed.

267
00:12:58,870 --> 00:13:01,870
[ATTENDANT] I have a message
from Empress Boraqchin.

268
00:13:01,950 --> 00:13:05,080
She's requested that Miss Fatima
come speak with her again.

269
00:13:06,710 --> 00:13:07,630
[Sitara grunts]

270
00:13:08,210 --> 00:13:09,170
[Töregene exhales]

271
00:13:09,290 --> 00:13:10,340
[SITARA (ADULT)]
The following year...

272
00:13:10,420 --> 00:13:11,590
MONGOLS - SOUTHERN SONG
KAIFENG JIN DYNASTY

273
00:13:11,670 --> 00:13:13,550
to ensure
the Jin capital of Kaifeng

274
00:13:13,630 --> 00:13:15,300
would be
completely surrounded,

275
00:13:15,470 --> 00:13:17,140
Tolui's army sought permission

276
00:13:17,220 --> 00:13:19,640
to pass through the lands
of the Southern Song.

277
00:13:19,720 --> 00:13:20,760
But instead...

278
00:13:21,810 --> 00:13:23,430
They killed our messenger?

279
00:13:24,060 --> 00:13:26,230
So that's the Southern Song's
response.

280
00:13:26,900 --> 00:13:28,190
Should we all turn back?

281
00:13:29,770 --> 00:13:30,820
Hardly.

282
00:13:30,900 --> 00:13:33,440
We'll proceed south
exactly as we planned.

283
00:13:33,530 --> 00:13:36,740
We've already received
their unfavorable reply.

284
00:13:37,160 --> 00:13:41,160
If we go, none of their people
will take this quietly.

285
00:13:42,410 --> 00:13:44,120
[Tolui scoffs] Well...

286
00:13:45,040 --> 00:13:47,420
we'll just have
to defeat them too.

287
00:13:47,920 --> 00:13:49,290
[soldiers shouting]

288
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:54,090
[groans]

289
00:13:58,430 --> 00:14:00,050
[all grunting]

290
00:14:05,430 --> 00:14:08,560
[SITARA (ADULT)] Tolui's army
breached the fortified pass,

291
00:14:08,690 --> 00:14:11,440
then continued along
the mountain roads.

292
00:14:13,400 --> 00:14:16,900
[TOLUI] These mountains prove
to be no match for us after all.

293
00:14:18,360 --> 00:14:20,870
The Great Kha'an
will be most pleased.

294
00:14:20,950 --> 00:14:21,870
Huh?

295
00:14:23,240 --> 00:14:25,040
Without question.

296
00:14:25,830 --> 00:14:28,830
I have no doubt my brother
will be overjoyed!

297
00:14:28,920 --> 00:14:31,960
[laughs]

298
00:14:32,040 --> 00:14:33,710
[sheep bleating]

299
00:14:38,130 --> 00:14:39,470
[SORGHAGHTANI] Dear God,

300
00:14:40,050 --> 00:14:42,760
please bless Tolui
and watch over him.

301
00:14:43,350 --> 00:14:46,480
[HULEGU] Come now, you know
Father would never lose.

302
00:14:46,560 --> 00:14:47,680
TOLUI'S SON
HULEGU

303
00:14:47,770 --> 00:14:49,390
Why even bother praying for him?

304
00:14:49,480 --> 00:14:52,570
My! How could you say that
before God?

305
00:14:53,320 --> 00:14:55,280
I feel confident
that my dear husband

306
00:14:55,360 --> 00:14:56,900
would never lose in battle.

307
00:14:57,450 --> 00:14:58,530
That said,

308
00:14:58,900 --> 00:15:02,410
misfortune can strike
outside of the battlefield.

309
00:15:02,490 --> 00:15:04,370
Those with too much power

310
00:15:04,450 --> 00:15:06,870
are viewed with great fear
and resentment.

311
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:09,410
Mother, then you
must be careful too.

312
00:15:09,870 --> 00:15:12,170
I must be? [giggles]

313
00:15:12,250 --> 00:15:15,250
No one would give me
any thought whatsoever.

314
00:15:18,630 --> 00:15:20,340
[HULEGU] I can only hope so.

315
00:15:22,140 --> 00:15:24,470
[sheep bleating]

316
00:15:24,600 --> 00:15:26,220
♪

317
00:15:32,520 --> 00:15:33,560
[Sitara grunts]

318
00:15:34,480 --> 00:15:35,820
[bells jingle]

319
00:15:39,280 --> 00:15:40,860
Here you are. [grunts]

320
00:15:41,030 --> 00:15:42,700
Thank you. Right there is fine.

321
00:15:42,780 --> 00:15:44,700
♪

322
00:16:01,130 --> 00:16:02,970
There, fresh off the pot.

323
00:16:03,390 --> 00:16:05,140
Thank you very much.

324
00:16:05,800 --> 00:16:08,600
I thought I'd bring you
some urum, Lady Töregene.

325
00:16:09,390 --> 00:16:11,520
[exclaims]
I love it the most now

326
00:16:11,600 --> 00:16:13,350
when it's at its ripest.

327
00:16:14,610 --> 00:16:15,820
[chuckles]

328
00:16:16,440 --> 00:16:18,070
So good.

329
00:16:18,150 --> 00:16:20,240
Autumn will soon be upon us,

330
00:16:20,360 --> 00:16:22,610
and the urum will be used
to make butter.

331
00:16:22,990 --> 00:16:24,950
This may be the last batch
of the season.

332
00:16:25,030 --> 00:16:26,950
You should have some as well.

333
00:16:27,030 --> 00:16:28,330
Oh, I couldn't.

334
00:16:28,410 --> 00:16:32,080
Besides, Empress Boraqchin
has just asked to speak with me.

335
00:16:32,160 --> 00:16:33,500
What, again?

336
00:16:33,580 --> 00:16:36,170
I'm sorry.
I should be going now.

337
00:16:36,250 --> 00:16:37,420
[Töregene sighs]

338
00:16:37,500 --> 00:16:38,750
♪

339
00:16:48,350 --> 00:16:50,560
That's all right by me.

340
00:16:54,020 --> 00:16:55,810
[SITARA]
In the natural world,

341
00:16:55,900 --> 00:16:58,900
substance and qualities
are very closely intermingled.

342
00:16:58,980 --> 00:17:01,530
By altering
its essential properties,

343
00:17:01,650 --> 00:17:04,610
one thing can be entirely
transformed into another.

344
00:17:05,160 --> 00:17:06,910
In much simpler terms,

345
00:17:06,990 --> 00:17:09,700
that is what this treatise
by Jabir is really all about.

346
00:17:10,490 --> 00:17:11,660
What does it mean?

347
00:17:11,750 --> 00:17:13,870
[BORAQCHIN] By understanding
an object's qualities,

348
00:17:13,960 --> 00:17:16,000
one can make whatever
is desired,

349
00:17:16,080 --> 00:17:18,000
whether that be a remedy
or a weapon.

350
00:17:18,130 --> 00:17:19,590
Oh, wow, amazing!

351
00:17:19,670 --> 00:17:21,590
Just look at sandarac.

352
00:17:21,670 --> 00:17:23,340
When rahj al-gar is heated,

353
00:17:23,420 --> 00:17:26,380
it immediately turns white
and becomes more toxic.

354
00:17:26,890 --> 00:17:29,430
They seem to have approached
the truth of this world,

355
00:17:29,510 --> 00:17:31,560
both, the scholars
of your homeland,

356
00:17:31,680 --> 00:17:33,600
and Daoists
of the Middle Kingdom.

357
00:17:34,020 --> 00:17:35,520
[Sitara gasps]

358
00:17:36,640 --> 00:17:39,570
[SITARA] The Great Kha'an
and Empress Boraqchin,

359
00:17:39,730 --> 00:17:41,030
they're thinking about
what happens

360
00:17:41,110 --> 00:17:43,070
after the Jin
have been conquered.

361
00:17:43,570 --> 00:17:46,240
And they're taking
a broader view of the world.

362
00:17:47,410 --> 00:17:48,320
Uh...

363
00:17:49,080 --> 00:17:50,030
[Sitara sighs]

364
00:17:50,120 --> 00:17:52,240
What's the matter?
Are you all right?

365
00:17:52,700 --> 00:17:55,330
[SITARA] Uh, well,
Lord Chinqai mentioned

366
00:17:55,410 --> 00:17:56,870
that he was struggling
with the shortage

367
00:17:56,960 --> 00:17:58,210
of scribes here.

368
00:17:59,130 --> 00:18:01,340
But I don't understand
how that could be.

369
00:18:01,420 --> 00:18:03,460
Haven't the Mongols
obtained people and knowledge

370
00:18:03,550 --> 00:18:04,960
from all over the world?

371
00:18:05,050 --> 00:18:06,720
-[BORAQCHIN] Mm.
-[MÖGE] Hm?

372
00:18:06,880 --> 00:18:09,100
The Mongols
have obtained intellectuals,

373
00:18:09,180 --> 00:18:10,970
but a great vast majority
of them...

374
00:18:11,470 --> 00:18:14,020
fall under
the House of Tolui's rule now.

375
00:18:14,100 --> 00:18:15,270
[Sitara gasps]

376
00:18:15,350 --> 00:18:16,640
Just like the military,

377
00:18:16,730 --> 00:18:19,310
Prince Tolui is entitled
as Otchigin.

378
00:18:19,440 --> 00:18:21,570
If that's true,
then couldn't the Great Kha'an

379
00:18:21,650 --> 00:18:23,320
just use his authority?

380
00:18:23,480 --> 00:18:24,480
Are you suggesting

381
00:18:24,570 --> 00:18:26,650
that he should pilfer
his own brother's property?

382
00:18:26,740 --> 00:18:28,910
I... I am sorry.

383
00:18:29,950 --> 00:18:32,580
There's an intellectual
imbalance as well?

384
00:18:33,700 --> 00:18:36,540
Actually, that should work
to our advantage.

385
00:18:37,910 --> 00:18:40,710
Do you truly believe
that would be for the best?

386
00:18:40,840 --> 00:18:41,750
[BOTH] Huh?

387
00:18:42,670 --> 00:18:44,840
[SITARA]
I can't help but feel afraid.

388
00:18:45,010 --> 00:18:48,590
The House of Tolui controls
military and intellectual might.

389
00:18:49,430 --> 00:18:50,970
Well, that only means...

390
00:18:51,050 --> 00:18:52,510
...that it is
even more important

391
00:18:52,600 --> 00:18:54,310
to work in tandem with them.
[chuckles]

392
00:18:56,060 --> 00:18:58,480
Does Prince Tolui
feel the same way, though?

393
00:18:58,560 --> 00:18:59,770
[MÖGE] Hmm.

394
00:19:00,310 --> 00:19:03,020
[BORAQCHIN] Möge, forgive me,
but could you leave us?

395
00:19:03,190 --> 00:19:04,110
[gasps softly]

396
00:19:12,070 --> 00:19:13,950
Till Möge brought you to us,

397
00:19:14,080 --> 00:19:15,410
I have no recollection

398
00:19:15,490 --> 00:19:17,290
of ever once
having seen you here before.

399
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:20,080
So who in the world are you?

400
00:19:21,380 --> 00:19:23,340
[SITARA] I'm sure you wouldn't
be familiar with me.

401
00:19:26,380 --> 00:19:29,970
After all, I was serving
as Princess Sorghaghtani's aide.

402
00:19:30,970 --> 00:19:32,890
I urge you to be cautious.

403
00:19:32,970 --> 00:19:34,930
She hasn't given up
on her ambition...

404
00:19:35,430 --> 00:19:38,560
to see Prince Tolui
become the Great Kha'an

405
00:19:38,640 --> 00:19:40,940
and for herself
to be the Great Khatun.

406
00:19:42,190 --> 00:19:43,400
[Boraqchin gasps]

407
00:19:44,690 --> 00:19:46,610
Sorghaghtani, you say?

408
00:19:48,780 --> 00:19:52,240
I see. I shall bear it
in mind then.

409
00:19:53,120 --> 00:19:55,030
But why have you suddenly chosen

410
00:19:55,120 --> 00:19:57,700
to divulge all this
to me, Fatima?

411
00:19:58,240 --> 00:20:01,160
I must warn you
to choose your answer wisely.

412
00:20:01,920 --> 00:20:04,340
[SITARA] It's all right.
I can do this.

413
00:20:04,420 --> 00:20:05,500
As of now,

414
00:20:05,590 --> 00:20:08,590
I have a fairly good sense
of what's going on in her mind.

415
00:20:09,710 --> 00:20:11,220
Truth be told,

416
00:20:11,340 --> 00:20:14,180
I don't have any idea
how she became Great Khatun.

417
00:20:15,220 --> 00:20:17,600
[SITARA] No matter how wise
this woman is,

418
00:20:17,680 --> 00:20:20,430
there must be many who think
as Lady Töregene does.

419
00:20:20,520 --> 00:20:23,850
People question how she came
to hold such authority,

420
00:20:24,310 --> 00:20:27,190
which is why she clings
so firmly to her own acumen.

421
00:20:27,940 --> 00:20:29,070
Simply put,

422
00:20:29,610 --> 00:20:31,110
you and Emperor Ögedei

423
00:20:31,190 --> 00:20:32,990
have filled me
with a sense of hope!

424
00:20:33,070 --> 00:20:33,990
[Boraqchin exclaims]

425
00:20:34,070 --> 00:20:36,370
[SITARA] The great wisdom
you both display

426
00:20:36,450 --> 00:20:39,450
makes you worthy of ruling
this world with honor and grace.

427
00:20:39,540 --> 00:20:40,450
Yes.

428
00:20:40,540 --> 00:20:41,790
♪

429
00:20:41,870 --> 00:20:43,960
[Boraqchin gasps]

430
00:20:45,960 --> 00:20:48,630
Do you really think so?

431
00:20:52,130 --> 00:20:53,930
Of course I do.

432
00:20:54,010 --> 00:20:55,930
[footsteps]

433
00:20:56,010 --> 00:20:58,720
[SITARA] I expected her
to be a fairly crafty one,

434
00:20:58,810 --> 00:21:00,770
but she was so easy to handle.

435
00:21:00,890 --> 00:21:03,310
I have to tell Lady Töregene
about this.

436
00:21:03,390 --> 00:21:05,400
-[FEMALE SLAVE] Excuse me!
-Uh?

437
00:21:05,480 --> 00:21:09,360
[pants] Um, I was attempting
to make butter,

438
00:21:09,480 --> 00:21:11,480
but I'm still not used to it,

439
00:21:11,690 --> 00:21:14,990
and I have plenty of milk.
You see, it's over there.

440
00:21:15,610 --> 00:21:17,450
I'd be glad to help.
Don't worry.

441
00:21:17,990 --> 00:21:20,410
[exclaims]
Thank you so very much.

442
00:21:20,580 --> 00:21:21,700
[female slave chuckles]

443
00:21:22,290 --> 00:21:24,830
Oh, Lady Töregene.

444
00:21:26,670 --> 00:21:27,920
Guess it can wait.

445
00:21:30,760 --> 00:21:32,340
[footsteps]

446
00:21:40,260 --> 00:21:42,270
[SITARA] Lady Töregene?

447
00:21:46,390 --> 00:21:47,810
[BORAQCHIN]
There's no need for you

448
00:21:47,900 --> 00:21:49,570
to feel so nervous.

449
00:21:50,400 --> 00:21:53,610
I just have something I wanted
to discuss with you.

450
00:21:58,070 --> 00:22:01,990
GREAT KHATUN BORAQCHIN

451
00:22:02,080 --> 00:22:05,290
[♪ closing theme song playing]

452
00:23:33,130 --> 00:23:35,340
[SITARA (ADULT)]
Next time. "Tengri."

453
00:23:35,460 --> 00:23:36,920
TENGRI

